From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:35:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] monitor: build Penguin's raw QMP event emitter

penguin_qmp_emit_event() (system/penguin.h) pushes an unsolicited QMP event
of any name to every connected QMP monitor: the outbound counterpart to the
QMP command callback. It walks mon_list the way monitor_qapi_event_emit()
does, so it needs monitor-internal.h and lives in monitor/penguin-event.c
(vendored) rather than beside the other hooks in system/penguin.c. This is
the only upstream file it touches: add it to the qmp source set.

Ported from rehosting/qemu 862d4fb74f (#22).

Co-authored-by: Benjamin Levy <153011444+be32826@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 monitor/meson.build | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/monitor/meson.build b/monitor/meson.build
index 4c58dd148c0496156b93feeb66cee2cfb27e07fd..b058dbca7040a68775d1d6ac9312b5d94307b12f 100644
--- a/monitor/meson.build
+++ b/monitor/meson.build
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
-qmp_ss.add(files('monitor.c', 'qmp.c', 'qmp-cmds-control.c'))
+qmp_ss.add(files('monitor.c', 'penguin-event.c', 'qmp.c',
+                 'qmp-cmds-control.c'))
 
 system_ss.add(files(
   'fds.c',
